# Maintainer: ArchMage contributors
#
# ArchMage desktop layer umbrella (DESKTOP-01, x86_64).
#
# Overlays-only (STRATEGY §4): configuration and meta wiring only; depends
# on upstream packages and sibling archmage-* packages, forks nothing.
#
# Phone-only packages are deliberately absent: cn-apn (modem APN),
# archmage-phosh-safety (phosh shell), archmage-fcitx5-osk (phosh OSK),
# waydroid stack (apps layer), archmage-btrfs-rollback (rollback layout
# follows the phone image's partition scheme). cn-mirror is ALARM-specific
# (archlinuxarm tree) — the desktop side gets its own x86_64 Arch mirror
# package in a follow-up (archmage-desktop-mirror).

pkgname=archmage-desktop
pkgver=1
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc='ArchMage desktop layer umbrella: CN defaults + management baseline (x86_64)'
arch=(x86_64)
url='https://github.com/Arcane-Reflection/ArchMage'
license=(Apache)
depends=(
  # CN defaults (arch-agnostic configuration packages)
  'archmage-cn-locale'
  'archmage-cn-fonts-meta'
  'archmage-cn-net'
  # NOTE: cn-mirror intentionally excluded — ALARM-specific mirrorlist.
  # TUI management layer rides here once the v0.2 milestone lands
  # (archmage dispatcher + gum/fzf; Phase 5 of ROADMAP.md).
)

package() {
    install -d "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname"
    cat > "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname/README" <<'DESCEOF'
ArchMage desktop layer umbrella.

Installs the CN-default configuration set that applies to x86_64 desktop
systems (locale, CJK fonts, network defaults). Phone-only layers (modem
APN, phosh shell safety, OSK, waydroid, btrfs rollback layout) are
deliberately not pulled in.

Management happens through the archmage TUI layer (see ROADMAP.md v0.2).
DESCEOF
}
